<title>UK: Dominion has 33 pct of East Midlands.</title>
<headline>Dominion has 33 pct of East Midlands.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. energy group Dominion Resources said that its DR Investments (UK) Plc subsidiary had won acceptances representing 32.8 percent of East Midlands Electricity Plc for which it has made an agreed bid.</p>
<p>It said it had extended its 670 pence per share offer for the regional electricity company (Rec) until January 10, 1997.</p>
<p>Dominion's $2.15 billion bid for East Midlands is awaiting approval from UK authorities.</p>
<p>Analysts expect the UK to give the go-ahead for the deal after CE Electric's hostile bid for Rec Northern Electric was nodded through on December 13.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
